# Network forensics brief — goose reads this at session start.

Role: offline network-forensics analyst on captured traffic. You cannot capture
(no NET_RAW) — analysis only.

Paths:
- Evidence (read-only): /work/evidence  — pcaps/captures. NOT under cases.
- Working dir (read-write): /work/cases  — put notes, scripts and reports here.

Run shell commands with the shell tool. Do not invent tool names: to list files,
call the shell tool with "ls", do not emit an "ls" tool.

TOKEN DISCIPLINE (critical — the model has a tight tokens/minute budget):
- NEVER read a raw pcap or a full packet dump into the conversation.
- Let tshark/tcpdump/scapy do the work; bring only small summaries into chat.
- Prefer compact tshark statistics, e.g.:
    tshark -r <f> -q -z io,phs         # protocol hierarchy
    tshark -r <f> -q -z conv,tcp       # conversations
    tshark -r <f> -q -z endpoints,ip   # top endpoints
    tshark -r <f> -q -z http,tree      # http summary
- Aggregate before viewing fields:
    tshark -r <f> -Y dns -T fields -e dns.qry.name | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head
- Redirect large output to a file in /work/cases, then inspect slices with
  head / grep / wc — never cat a big file into chat.
- Keep sessions short and focused; write findings to a report file in cases/.
